WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.470
At low tide in a sheltered estuary, the
water drains away from a wide plain of

2
00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:06.730
bare mud.

3
00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:11.390
It looks lifeless, but it teems
with worms and mud-snails,

4
00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:14.490
food for waders such as knot and dunlin.

5
00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:18.110
Yet some plants, such as
glasswort, take root here,

6
00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:20.910
on mud the tide keeps covering.

7
00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:25.090
Further up the shore, livestock
graze a green salt meadow.

8
00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:30.310
So how does bare, sticky mud turn
into a meadow that cattle can graze?

9
00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:33.690
In this mission, you'll
read a marsh plant by plant,

10
00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:36.050
from the seaward edge to the meadow.

11
00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:41.590
Then you'll see how people rewrote the
story by planting cord-grass on mudflats.

12
00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:46.840
Your mission: explain how bare estuary
mud becomes a grazed salt meadow.
